==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[chalk]] [[up]]|chalks up|chalking up|chalked up}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[attribute]], [[credit]], or [[blame]].
#: '''''Chalk''' it '''up''' to inexperience, I guess, but he made a very poor decision.''
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} to [[achieve]] something
#* '''2012''' The Economist, Sep 29th 2012 issue, ''[http://www.economist.com/node/21563780 Rural activism: Working the system]''
#*: In recent years Mr Li, a divorced farmer with a laptop and internet access, has '''chalked up''' some [[stunning]] successes in resisting his village officials.

